# Root .dockerignore
#
# Applies to builds whose context is the REPO ROOT — i.e. the API image
# (apps/api-nest/Dockerfile and apps/api-nest/Dockerfile.dev).
#
# NOTE: the web image builds with `context: ./apps/web`. A subdirectory context
# does NOT read this file, so apps/web/.dockerignore governs that build
# independently.
#
# Rule order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins.
#
# Both a bare pattern and a `**/` form are listed for the security-critical
# entries, because the nested `**/` form is what guarantees a file inside a
# subdirectory (e.g. apps/api-nest/.env) is actually excluded.

# --- Secrets: must never reach the build context -------------------------
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
firebase-service-account.json
**/firebase-service-account.json
*-service-account.json
**/*-service-account.json
*serviceAccount*.json
**/*serviceAccount*.json
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
id_rsa*
**/id_rsa*
data/
**/data/

# --- VCS / editor / CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.turbo

# --- Dependencies and build output (regenerated inside the image) --------
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/bin
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/.vite-temp
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Frozen Go backend ---------------------------------------------------
# Archived per ADR 002; not part of any Node image. Excluding it also drops
# its compiled bin/server and local data/ from the build context.
apps/api-legacy

# --- Local state ---------------------------------------------------------
backups/
tmp/
temp/
*.log
